# Monument to Endurance: "whenever you discard a card, choose one that hasn't been chosen this turn". Turn 1: Faithless
# Looting discards two Plains together, two triggers, one for each card (CR 603.2c); the first takes "draw a card" and
# the second, with that mode spent as it went on the stack (CR 603.3c), "create a Treasure token". The Treasure casts a
# Masked Meower, whose discard leaves only "each opponent loses 3 life" (taken without asking): Bot2 to 17. A second
# Meower, off Mox Ruby, discards a fourth card: every mode is spent, so nothing goes on the stack beside the Meower's own
# ability (CR 700.2). Turn 2: Bot2's own Faithless Looting is not Bot1 discarding, and triggers nothing. Turn 3: the modes are fresh again, and a third Meower's discard drains Bot2 to 14.

